I have enough durable context. Let me record my pre-work notes.

**Pre-work assessment (required notes):**
1. **What the system is trying to learn:** to reliably separate genuine, cost-survivable quantitative edges from noise, and to improve the process that chooses which such questions to test.
2. **Current binding constraint:** the only candidate positive evidence (short-horizon momentum, lookbacks 3/5/10) has never been costed; execution-cost robustness is the remaining decision-relevant qualification.
3. **Uncertainty blocking a better decision:** whether the ~0.05–0.13 median log-return edge is an artifact of a zero-cost fill model (a 2x-notional daily flip must pay the spread/commission).
4. **Single bounded action:** run a predeclared, a-priori cost grid (realistic baseline, 2x stress, zero-cost reference) × lookback {3,5,10} × 10 assets through the existing walk-forward/regime gate with a matched cost-aware coin-flip null, then independently recompute.
5. **Why worth it:** bounded (reuses existing framework, one new check + one verifier), falsifiable in either direction, and it settles whether the campaign's sole positive candidate belongs in the evidence base.
