@@ -900,16 +900,30 @@
 produces uniformly negative results, the momentum variant should
 produce uniformly positive results; either outcome settles whether the
 5-day-lookback direction bet is a robust edge on this universe.
 
+Signal timing (defect fixed 2026-11-22, campaign slot 02): the return is
+``closes[i] / closes[i - lookback] - 1``, evaluated at the close of bar
+``i``. That bar's close is the fill price for the position established at
+bar ``i`` and held into bar ``i + 1``, so the signal uses no information
+beyond its own bar. The prior implementation used
+``mean(log(closes[i - lookback + 1 : i + 1]))``, which is the mean log
+*price level* over the window, not a return: its sign compares the mean
+price with a fixed zero level, so on a universe whose prices are far above
+zero it is almost always positive and the signal degenerates into an
+almost-always-long buy-and-hold bet (measured: one position flip in 4465
+bars on 9/10 collected assets). That defect produced the "momentum"
+verdicts recorded in earlier activations; it is corrected here rather than
+preserved, and the old verdicts are retracted in `state/STATE.md`.
+
 No look-ahead: each signal uses only closes up to and including its own
 bar.
 """
 n = len(closes)
 out: List[Signal] = [Signal(date=i + 1, weight=0.0) for i in range(n)]
 lookback = int(lookback)
 for i in range(lookback, n):
-    ret = float(np.mean(np.log(closes[i - lookback + 1 : i + 1])))
+    ret = float(closes[i] / closes[i - lookback] - 1.0)
     out[i] = Signal(date=i + 1, weight=1.0 if ret > 0 else -1.0)
 return out
 
 

